{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105295","id":2455061359,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6SVUNv","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105295","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105295.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105295.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105295","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105295/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105295/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105295/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/eb101c2bc9b864dcb831830b4bf59ecb0f5341dc","number":105295,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add `Color.to_named`","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Proposal: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12178.\r\n\r\nAdds a method to `Color` called `to_named` which returns the (mathematically-) closest standardized color name to the color.\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar white = Color(1, 1, 1, 0.5)\r\nprint(white.to_named()) # Prints \"WHITE\"\r\n```\r\n```csharp\r\nvar white = new Color(1, 1, 1, 0.5f);\r\nGD.Print(white.ToNamed()); // Prints \"WHITE\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe implementation loops through each standardized color and tracks the closest color by subtracting the components and calculating the squared distance.\r\n\r\n### Performance\r\n\r\n#### C++\r\n\r\nAccording to an external benchmark by @Ivorforce, the worst-case of the C++ function takes about 0.09 microseconds (0.00000009 seconds) (omitting the `String` allocation) meaning it could be called over 185,000 times per frame at 60FPS.\r\n\r\n#### C#\r\n\r\nAccording to an external benchmark by myself, the worst-case of the C# function takes about 0.351 microseconds (0.000000351 seconds) meaning it could be called over 47,000 times per frame at 60FPS:\r\n\r\n| Method                | Mean       | Error     | StdDev    |\r\n|---------------------- |-----------:|----------:|----------:|\r\n| DictionaryWorst       | 467.159 ns | 1.6780 ns | 1.4012 ns |\r\n| FrozenDictionaryWorst | 351.904 ns | 1.8579 ns | 1.7379 ns |\r\n| DictionaryBest        |   5.752 ns | 0.0251 ns | 0.0235 ns |\r\n| FrozenDictionaryBest  |   5.366 ns | 0.0220 ns | 0.0205 ns |\r\n\r\nThe `Frozen` benchmarks refer to #105104.\r\n\r\n## Potential Issues\r\n\r\n### Returned case\r\n\r\n**IMPORTANT**: Currently, since the C# dictionary keys are in `UPPERFLATCASE`, there is no way to convert to a different case. So that should be fixed, but it's a separate issue.\r\n\r\nThe C++ case keys are currently in `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` meaning that would be returned here. However, the user is unlikely to want that case. It can be converted to another case for example `Title Case` (the case used by X11) using a string function like `Capitalize`, although that would result in more allocations.\r\n\r\n### English-only (no translations)\r\n\r\nThe returned color name would be in English only, without options to translate to another language.\r\n\r\nSince the other functions relating to color names are English-only anyway, this would likely be fine (as stated by @Zireael07 in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12178#issuecomment-2797141221).\r\n\r\nHowever, since this function would almost certainly be used for displaying colors to the user rather than accepting colors on the programming side, it could be a bigger issue with this function.\r\n\r\n### Performance\r\n\r\n@Calinou suggested a faster version of this method would be:\r\n\r\n> to create a 3D LUT using a palette that matches the web colors only, and sampling this 3D LUT on the CPU according to the color and return the color (which will always match a web color exactly).\r\n\r\nHowever, since this function is so performant already, and its main use cases would only call it rarely, this optimisation was considered unnecessary by myself and @Ivorforce.\r\n\r\n- _Bugsquad edit: closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12178_","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 releas